course: dictionary
lesson: 15744
title: Treachery and trust
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Treachery is a noun. It means betraying someone who trusts you, or being disloyal and false. You can often work out its meaning from the words around it. «Tom told his best friend's secret to the whole class. Everyone was shocked by his treachery.» His friend trusted him, and Tom broke that trust, so treachery means betrayal.
explain: Treachery can also mean a hidden danger. «The lake looked calm, but the treachery of the thin ice nearly sent Lily under.» The ice looked safe, but it was not. The clue is nearly sent under: something that seemed safe was really dangerous.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does "Tom's betrayal shocked everyone" still make sense? Yes, so betrayal is a good meaning. If your swapped meaning does not fit, read the sentence again and look for clues.
fact: Treachery means betraying someone who trusts you.
fact: Treachery can also mean a hidden danger, like the treachery of thin ice.
fact: The opposite of treachery is loyalty, which means staying true to a friend or cause.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the weasels and stoats take Toad Hall while Toad is away, and this is a story of treachery.
fact: The Gunpowder Plot was a famous plot of betrayal against King James I, and traitors are people who commit treachery.
exercise: «Tom told his best friend's secret to the whole class. His treachery shocked everyone.» What does treachery mean here? | Being very tall and strong | Winning a race | *Betraying someone who trusts you | Playing a fair game
exercise: «The lake looked calm, but the treachery of the thin ice nearly sent Lily under.» What does treachery mean here? | A friendly warning | *A hidden danger that looks safe | A soft, warm blanket
exercise: Treachery is the opposite of which word? | Laughter | *Loyalty | Rudeness | Hunger
test: In The Wind in the Willows, what is the treachery? | Toad inviting his friends to a dinner party | Mole planting a garden | *The weasels and stoats taking Toad Hall while Toad is away | Rat writing a poem
test: Which sentence shows treachery? | A friend shares their lunch with you | A friend waves hello at the gate | *A friend tells your secret to everyone after promising to keep it | A friend helps you carry your heavy bag
exam: «The guard let the thieves in after promising to watch the gate. His ____ was discovered by the king.» | *treachery | kindness | laughter | courage
